Implemented: Zero-Touch Mobile Auto-Connect on Same Wi-Fi
The app is now configured so that once installed on your phone and connected to the same Wi-Fi as your TV, it automatically detects, connects, and controls your Fire TV devices without you needing to manually connect every time.

How the Mobile Auto-Connect Engine Works
1. Persistent Device Memory (localStorage):
    * The app saves your paired TV and Stick IPs in persistent storage.
    * When you open the app on your phone, it immediately checks your local network and locks onto your Fire TV devices.
    * You don't have to re-enter IPs or press connect every time you open the app.
2. Zero-Touch Background Wi-Fi Discovery (mobileAutoConnect.ts):
    * On app startup, DRemote automatically detects your local Wi-Fi subnet (e.g., 192.168.1.x, 192.168.0.x, 10.0.0.x) via WebRTC local address probing.
    * It performs a rapid background sweep on standard Fire TV ports (8008 DIAL, 8009 Fling, 8080, and 5555).
    * If your router reassigns your Fire TV's IP address (DHCP drift), DRemote discovers the new IP in the background and updates it automatically.
3. Direct Multi-Channel Remote Dispatch:
    * When you press any remote button on your phone (D-pad arrows, Select, Home, Back, Menu, Volume, Power, or App shortcuts), commands are dispatched across available local channels:
        1. Direct Fire TV DIAL HTTP (http://<ip>:8008/apps/...) for native app launches and system intents.
        2. Direct Fire TV WebSocket (ws://<ip>:8008 and ws://<ip>:8080).
        3. Local Bridge / Express Backend for zero-lag physical ADB keyevents (input keyevent <code}>).
    * Dispatches seamlessly without blocking UI responsiveness.
4. Instant Visual & Haptic Feedback on Mobile:
    * Click Sounds: Tactile audio click on every button press.
    * Haptic Vibration: Physical vibration feedback on Android and iOS devices.
    * Alexa Cyan LED Ring: The glow ring at the top of the remote pulses with every keystroke.
    * Live TV Visual Monitor: Tap the TV icon in the header to view an interactive on-screen TV monitor showing current HDMI inputs, active streaming apps (Netflix, YouTube, Prime Video, Disney+), cursor positions, and hardware volume OSD bars.
5. PWA Standalone Installation:
    * Tap the Install App button in the header (or "Add to Home Screen" in your mobile browser) to install DRemote as a native standalone app on your phone.
    * When launched from your home screen on your home Wi-Fi, the status header immediately displays 🟢 Wi-Fi Linked and ● Live Bridge Connected.
